/**
 * dfcFaceUpDerive.test.js — the layer derive reads a multi-face permanent's FACE THAT IS UP (CR 712.8d), never its combined
 * "Front // Back" type line (2026-10-16).
 *
 * THE BUG. In-game cards carry Scryfall's combined type line (cardIndex.publicCard keeps `type_line`). The layer derive
 * (layers.cardTypesOf / subtypesOf) took the card types left of the line's FIRST dash and the subtypes right of it, so a front
 * face printed without a subtype took the back face's types: Westvale Abbey ("Land // Legendary Creature — Demon") derived as
 * [Land, //, Legendary, Creature] with a null front-face power and toughness — a 0/0 creature the toughness state-based action
 * (CR 704.5f) put into the graveyard the moment it was played as the land drop. Casting Heirloom Mirror did the same. All 20
 * permanent cards of that shape in the bundled snapshot died on entry; the back faces' subtypes rode along on every other
 * double-faced, adventure and flip permanent (Delver of Secrets was an Insect, an Invasion battle an Elemental), and a land
 * back made Treasure Map a land.
 *
 * THE RULE. A double-faced permanent with its front face up has only its front face's characteristics (CR 712.8d, 712.8f);
 * one put onto the battlefield enters front face up (CR 712.14); an adventurer has only its normal characteristics there (CR
 * 715.4); a copy copies the face that is up (CR 707.8). The engine never turns a back face up, so every combined permanent is
 * its front face (layers.faceUpTypeLine).
 *
 * THE MASK IT LIFTED. Halvar, God of Battle // Sword of the Realms sits on the battlefield as the combined card, whose text
 * carries the back face's "Equip {1}{W}". The bleed made Halvar an Equipment creature, so the CR 301.5c guard refused its
 * attach by accident. Front face up, Halvar is a God and no Equipment; CR 701.3b ("an object that isn't an Aura, Equipment,
 * or Fortification ... doesn't move") now refuses it on purpose (layers.cannotEquipNow) — in the Equip resolver
 * (equipOfferParity.test.js), the attach-pair atom (Brass Squire, below) and the AI's equip pick.
 *
 * Real oracle fixtures: the bundled snapshot through cardIndex.publicCard + learnDeckEnrich.mergeCardData (a game deck card's
 * shape), generated 2026-10-16. The land drops and casts come from legalActionsForPlayer, dispatchAction applies them, and the
 * stack resolves through resolveTopOfStack / finalizeStackResolution (the state-based actions run there).
 */
